From: TefMeister <td3kxlvr@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:23:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Two-handed long guns: aim the shot down the line between
 the hands

TwoHandedAim, a bool a mod sets on the player. When it is on and the off hand
is tracked, the shot follows the hand-to-hand line instead of the rear
controller's own tilt. Two guards (least separation, agreement with where the
gun points); refusing leaves aiming exactly as it was.

Both guard numbers are settings rather than constants (vr_two_handed_min_sep,
vr_two_handed_max_disagree) with sliders in VR Options, plus
vr_two_handed_debug which prints which guard refused -- so the first headset
session can tune them without a rebuild.

The maths is two_handed_aim.h, unchanged from the tested copy (36/36 checks).

