From c56087c3a5e3d7bcc75c1686d36090feca88d2a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TefMeister <td3kxlvr@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:21:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Two-handed long guns: DRAW the gun along the line between
 the hands

The shot already followed the hand-to-hand line; the gun itself never did. It
stayed glued to the weapon controller, so from inside the headset a working
change looked like nothing at all -- the barrel did not move, and the off hand
appeared to do nothing.

GetWeaponTransform now rebuilds the weapon pose: the rear hand keeps the gun's
position and the twist of the wrist, and the off hand sets which way the barrel
points, however far apart the hands are. openvr_weaponRotate is folded into the
frame the barrel direction replaces rather than applied on top of it.

MapAttackDir and the per-tic AttackPos block take the new GetWeaponTransformRaw
instead. AttackAngle/AttackPitch are already turned onto the hand line by the
aim block, so feeding them the re-aimed matrix as well would apply the same turn
twice.

New setting vr_two_handed_draw (on, Options -> VR Options) turns it off for
comparison. Anything missing -- no off hand, no player, hands in the same place
-- falls back to the one-handed transform, so the worst case is the behaviour
the engine had before.

Maths in two_handed_pose.h; 103 checks in the Ashes repo, and five deliberate
breakages all caught.

