From f3815e7b6d02ac825fa328951c6ce376cca3785b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TefMeister <td3kxlvr@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:18:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Two-handed long guns: the SHOT follows the drawn barrel
 as well

Worn 2026-09-20: the gun turns with the off hand, and the bullets did not -
they still left along the rear controller.

That was my own doing, one commit earlier. A shot''s direction comes from the
weapon matrix inside MapAttackDir, not from AttackAngle/AttackPitch: the yaw
and pitch handed in are the actor''s plus the weapon''s spread, and subtracting
the actor''s own angles leaves just that spread, so with no spread the answer is
exactly the matrix''s forward axis. I had pointed MapAttackDir at the RAW
one-handed matrix on the belief that the aim block''s AttackAngle would
otherwise be applied twice. Nothing on a bullet''s path reads AttackAngle, so
there was no double application - only a gun aimed one way and bullets going
another.

MapAttackDir now takes the same two-handed matrix the gun is drawn with, so the
bullet leaves the barrel you can see, by construction.

AttackAngle/AttackPitch are now derived from that same matrix too. Nothing on
the bullet path reads them, but a mod does - the laser sight - and a laser that
disagrees with the barrel is worse than none. The older tha::decide block stays
as the fallback for when vr_two_handed_draw is off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
